# ---- a mode's own screen (item 164): the scene lookup's typed finders (find_node casts to Radium::Sprite,
# find_text to Radium::Text; found through the lookup, Godzilla LE 1.16 0x587bac, by the class each casts to),
# the node's set-visible (Sprite slot 42) and the scene inside a scene player
site find_text        0x00484eb8 0xe92d4070 0xe24dd008
# Insider Connected score gate (item 166): the request header constructor (the endpoint in r1) and the
# message-begin thunk every sender calls next; the runtime refuses the score reports there
# (MODE_SDK.md, "Insider Connected: no score leaves a machine that carries modes")
site agent_header     0x004d2568 0xe92d40f8 0xe2505000
site agent_begin      0x004dced4 0xe590c004 0xe1a00001

# ---- a mode's own screen goes in this scene: drawn every frame of a game (item 164, the RadiumScene census)
scene hud                  2c8ffcac48035d12ef91df61fb7a796ec391f1e7

# ---- the framework's count of the balls in play (The Beatles 1.29 0x1fd194, found here by its code,
# 20/20 words alike); two or more is a multiball (the stack section) and a multiball of the mode's own
# watches it (item 167)
site balls_in_play         0x001712a4 0xe92d4010 0xe3094e3c

# ---- a multiball of the mode's own (item 167): the framework's start-a-multiball (The Beatles 1.29
# 0x1fd310, found here by its code, 24/24 words alike): serve balls until r0 are in play, r1 0, r2 the
# ball save in ticks (62 a second), r3 0xbb as this build's own multiballs pass it, two zero words on the
# stack. pm_multiball_start / pm_multiball_add; a mode file's `multiball` line; the tab's Multiball.
site multiball_serve       0x00171420 0xe92d41f0 0xe309ef4a
